### Explicit answers for zimmTextInput

| Capability | Supported? | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| **label** | **Yes, required** (`label: string`) | Renders `<chakra.label htmlFor={inputId}>` |
| **floating label** | **Yes** | `filled`/`focused` are fed back into `useMultiStyleConfig` so the recipe resolves the floated-label position; docblock: "flush text input with floating label" |
| **error / invalid message** | **Yes** | `errorText?: string` → `<chakra.p role="alert" id={errorId}>`, sets `aria-invalid={hasError}` and joins `errorId` into `aria-describedby` |
| **helper text** | **Yes** | `helperText?: string` → `<chakra.p id={helperId}>`, joined into `aria-describedby`. Note: unlike ZimmDropdown, helper is **not** suppressed when an error is present — both render |
| **required marker** | **NO** | No `required`/`isRequired` prop, no asterisk, no `aria-required` anywhere in the file |
| **disabled** | **Yes** | `disabled?: boolean` → native `disabled` on the input, fed to the recipe, and suppresses the clear button |
| **type (email/password/tel)** | **Partially** | `type?: string` — a free-form string passed straight to the input, so `email`/`password`/`tel` all "work", but there is **no union type constraining them and no per-type behaviour** except one special case: `autoComplete={type === 'email' ? 'email' : undefined}`. There is **no password show/hide toggle** (the `password` icon exists in `ZimmIcon` but is not used here) |
| **Chakra `FormControl`/`FormLabel`/`FormErrorMessage`** | **NO — none of them** | Imports only `chakra, useMultiStyleConfig` from `@chakra-ui/react`. Hand-rolls `chakra.div` / `chakra.label` / `chakra.input` / `chakra.p` and wires `useId()`-derived ids to `aria-describedby`/`aria-invalid` manually |

Other notes: value state is delegated to `useZimmTextInputState` (`app/hooks/useZimmTextInputState`) and supports both controlled (`value` + `onChange`) and uncontrolled (`defaultValue`) modes. `onChange` signature is `(value: string) => void` — **not** a React event handler. No `onBlur`/`onFocus`/`placeholder`/`maxLength`/`readOnly`/`autoFocus`/`id`/`inputRef`/`aria-label` props are exposed.

